  <Docs>
    <summary>
            Raised when <see cref="M:Azure.AI.AgentServer.Core.Streaming.AgentEventStream.EmitAsync(System.Net.ServerSentEvents.SseItem{System.String},System.Boolean,System.Threading.CancellationToken)" /> is called after the stream
            has been closed. This signals a producer bug (the producer should not emit
            after closing); HTTP layers should treat it as a server error (5xx), not a
            client error. Mirrors Python's <c>EventStreamClosedError</c>.
            </summary>
